                <pb facs="0224" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/111: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Charge of the Legation in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-26T15:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                                1919, 3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            December 27, 9.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>In accordance with recommendation in the Department’s cablegram of December 11, 3
                    p.m., the Honduranean Government gave instructions ten days ago to remove
                    telegraph office in disputed territory.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
